Cell["\<\
Every initial field therefore reaches its exact mean after the stated \
schedule. This exceptional finite-time consensus should not be extrapolated \
to arbitrary N: pair averaging has a dyadic denominator obstruction, and \
(0,0,1) cannot reach its mean after a finite word of pair averages.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "ConsensusBoundary", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 LineSpacing->{1.15, 2},
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "ConsensusBoundary"},ExpressionUUID->"a0f2d85b-35a2-241c-4d4e-\
80129417816e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Interpretation limits", "Section",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|"ID" -> "SectionLimits", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "SectionLimits"},ExpressionUUID->"c69b47a3-6384-069b-a2a5-a56b38c9124f"],

Cell["\<\
The executable transcript supports the following precise conclusions.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitsPositiveIntro", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 LineSpacing->{1.15, 2},
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitsPositiveIntro"},ExpressionUUID->"3c98c9c5-eb08-294a-4930-\
99400c876d7a"],

Cell["\<\
Pair averaging is an orthogonal projection with exact variance loss.\
\>", "Item",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitPositive1", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitPositive1"},ExpressionUUID->"e7fb1dcb-14bd-b2fb-fdd1-b6308f7d263c"],

Cell["Each Rule-A row contains exactly 3N resolution slots.", "Item",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitPositive2", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitPositive2"},ExpressionUUID->"c4d79000-e07d-f457-9ffe-9138d377b418"],

Cell["The N=4 Rule-A class law is nonuniform.", "Item",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitPositive3", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitPositive3"},ExpressionUUID->"cf6ebdbe-4352-c18c-a5ce-c8268f7f405d"],

Cell["\<\
Fixed-clock Rule B is symmetric and has uniform class stationarity.\
\>", "Item",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitPositive4", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitPositive4"},ExpressionUUID->"51df2809-8135-8b74-9a44-fb85e1d04ed3"],

Cell["\<\
Diffusion is exact rational matrix evolution, and the K4/Q3 schedules are \
exact finite consensus words.\
\>", "Item",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitPositive5", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitPositive5"},ExpressionUUID->"e7c6fa4b-253f-31c0-bbcf-8115c9eff3ef"],

Cell["There are also three important non-conclusions.", "Text",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitsNegativeIntro", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 LineSpacing->{1.15, 2},
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitsNegativeIntro"},ExpressionUUID->"4dc86d3f-7f45-e33a-bc1c-\
95282de2ff71"],

Cell["\<\
The bundled quotient model omits carrier edges, resolution identifiers, and \
settlement permutations, so it cannot by itself produce a pathwise \
transported field or Lyapunov exponent.\
\>", "ItemNumbered",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitNegative1", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitNegative1"},ExpressionUUID->"d9782e38-7f6b-596e-5192-6d1a0e595781"],

Cell["\<\
A single sampled trajectory does not approximate the exact distribution.\
\>", "ItemNumbered",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitNegative2", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitNegative2"},ExpressionUUID->"2d6f4b82-e61a-35c4-f5ab-b1e32239bd36"],

Cell["\<\
Complete finite checks through N=6 here or N=14 in the Python tables do not \
prove an asymptotic spectral or mixing statement.\
\>", "ItemNumbered",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "GoGComputationalNotes" -> <|
    "ID" -> "LimitNegative3", "Generated" -> True|>|>,
 FontSize->12,
 CellTags->{
  "GoGComputationalNotes", 
   "LimitNegative3"},ExpressionUUID->"6c2d6f59-add0-7580-e43e-d38847099097"]
}, Open  ]],

